==Swedish==
{{wikipedia|lang=sv}}

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|sv|/²vɛkːa/}}
* {{homophones|sv|väcka}}
* {{rhymes|sv|²ɛka|s=2}}

===Etymology 1===
From {{inh|sv|gmq-osw|vika}}, from {{inh|sv|non|vika}}, from {{inh|sv|gem-pro|*wikǭ}}, from {{der|sv|ine-pro|*weyg-||to bend, wind, turn, yield}}.

====Noun====
{{sv-noun|c}}

# a [[week]], a period of 7 days
#: {{ux|sv|Det går sju dagar på en '''vecka'''.|There are seven days in a '''week'''.}}
# a numbered period, ranging from 1 to 52 or 53, containing seven days beginning with Monday and ending with Sunday
#: {{synonyms|sv|v.}}
#: {{hypernyms|sv|datum}}
#: {{ux|sv|Vattnet kommer tillfälligt stängas av på torsdag '''vecka''' 35 pga underhållsarbete.|The water supply will be temporarily turned off on Thursday '''week''' 35 due to maintenance.}}

=====Usage notes=====
* Compounds are formed with vecko-, an archaic genitive.

